 {:seon.task/name "old-evaluations-collapse-in-chunks"
  :seon.task/plan "What exists: past `:seon.config.render/history-budget`, the history cut in `seon.context/request` drops the oldest record on every turn, so the message after the run sections changes each request and the scrollback misses the provider's prefix cache from then on. Field: SWE-agent's collapse of all but the last 5 observations beat full history by 3 points; Anthropic reports clearing old tool results as the lightest compaction; Manus keeps the context append-only. Correct: at the boundary, collapse the evaluations of all turns but the last N (a config key) to one line each (the form, its status, `(nth (my.turn/evals) k)`), once, so the collapsed prefix stays fixed for the following turns. Measure: cache-hit share per turn from turn 8 on, and turns to green on long runs."
